WEBVTT

00:00:00.625 --> 00:00:04.561
Private investing is inherently unstructured.

00:00:04.561 --> 00:00:14.113
Data comes from different sources, different places, and a lot of time is spent structuring this data.

00:00:14.113 --> 00:00:20.311
In the operational flow of a VC, there are different phases.

00:00:20.311 --> 00:00:32.658
In pre-screening alone, analysts spend time on different tasks to screen every pitch that comes in each month.

00:00:32.658 --> 00:00:39.739
What we've built so far is an AI analyst that solves the pre-call intelligence layer.

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:46.413
It takes data from the sources the VC fund already uses.

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:48.710
Let's say a deck comes in.

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:52.505
From the deck, key information is extracted.

00:00:52.505 --> 00:00:54.356
Claims are verified.

00:00:54.356 --> 00:00:58.016
Data is enriched from external sources.

00:00:58.016 --> 00:01:03.588
All of this runs inside the tools your fund already uses.

00:01:03.588 --> 00:01:20.785
The deck triggers a Slack notification with a summary, opens into a pre-call brief with a score, and syncs the deal into your CRM or Google Sheet — automatically.

00:01:20.785 --> 00:01:28.536
You can also interact with every deck the fund has received over time.

00:01:28.536 --> 00:01:34.043
This becomes a persistent, personalised context for the fund.

00:01:34.043 --> 00:01:45.915
As these operations get automated, a context graph is built — the institutional memory for private investors.

00:01:45.915 --> 00:01:47.351
We are hizen.

00:01:47.351 --> 00:01:54.634
We are building the intelligence layer for private investing.
